.TH MODLIST 10 "October 2026" "1.1" "Neverdark Manual"
.SH NAME
modlist \- List the modules loaded in a region
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modlist
.RI [ region ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
List the game modules loaded in a region: the region header first, then one
module stem per line.
.PP
The region is a bare world number (0\-65535) or the keyword \fBcosmos\fP,
under exactly the same rules as every other region selector. Without one the
command acts on your \fBdefault target region\fP (see \fBtarget\fP(10)), or
on the region you are standing in if you have set none. Regions at other
widths (see \fBgrant\fP(10)) are reached through your default; see
\fBtarget\fP(10) for the width\-and\-point form. A region with no row
answers that there is no such region.
.PP
Unlike its sibling commands this one has no ownership gate: any player may
list any existing region's module set. What runs where is public record;
changing it is what \fBloadmod\fP and \fBunloadmod\fP are for.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR loadmod,unloadmod,target,here,planet (10)
.SH AUTHOR
quirinpa <quirinpa@tty.pt>
